https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/nervous-system/peripheral-nervous-system/glossopharyngeal-nerve/21110

= The Pathology of General Paresis by William Henry Octavius Sankey
{parent=Neuroscience bibliography}
{c}
{title2=January 1864}
{tag=Work by William Henry Octavius Sankey}

https://doi.org/10.1192/bjp.9.48.467

Journal of Mental Science 9(48), pp. 467–493. The primary opening explicitly adopts the term general paresis to avoid confusion with general paralysis. The original printed date is distinguished from the 2018 digital publication date. The full article was not required for the claim made here.

= Non-traumatic Hematomyelia: A Rare Finding in Clinical Practice
{parent=Neuroscience bibliography}
{c}

https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6346806/

Primary case report, 2019. Introduction and clinical discussion describe pain, myotomal signs, causes and variable time course. No patient findings are transferred to the examination.

= German Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Treatment of Neurosyphilis (2020)
{parent=Neuroscience bibliography}
{c}

https://doi.org/10.1186/s42466-020-00081-1

General paresis, tabes dorsalis and diagnostic framework; not a description of what was proved in 1864.

